{
  "what": "A score fixture shaped like a real orchestral part. Synthetic \u2014 not a transcription of any page.",
  "why": "Every other fixture here is a simple exercise-book page: quarters and eighths, one metre, almost no rests. Measured by tools/engraver-coverage.py they made the engraver look adequate at 95% coverage, right up until the first part out of a real folder rendered as nothing at all. This is what such a page is made of \u2014 sections in different metres, runs of sixteenths, dotted march rhythms, a multi-bar rest, triplets and a written rit. What it is for is having something in the corpus that the corpus was missing.",
